      "writtenOn": "2023-03-09T10:21:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The default 0 means \"don\u0027t apply a timeout\", so doesn\u0027t this increase the chance of the test being killed? cs/android-internal/tools/tradefederation/core/test_framework/com/android/tradefed/testtype/HostTest.java?rcl\u003da3842433f2285b92a67f83649746cea5e9e17670\u0026l\u003d702\n\nThere\u0027s other timeouts involved, I think, but I\u0027m not sure they can be overridden from here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "18647792c872dd4bb8fd6c35a81d558fac96d3c2",
